WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.490
We all know Hagrid is the paragon of gentle
giants.

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:07.250
But can the same be said for the late actor
who played him – Robbie Coltrane?

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.950
HBO Max rang in 2022 with an incredible release
for fans, debuting a "Harry Potter" reunion

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.950
special featuring all of your favorite actors
and plenty of reminiscing about what it was

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.980
like to make this epic eight-film franchise.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.210
In particular, the younger set of actors who
grew up on the set had a lot of revelations

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:28.330
about what it was like to work with the adult
cast members, many of whom are some of the

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:32.349
most decorated performers in British film
and television history.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:37.140
From Maggie Smith to Helena Bonham Carter
to actors who sadly passed away like Richard

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.250
Harris, Richard Griffiths, and Alan Rickman,
the then-child actors had the opportunity

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.079
to work with some of the best living actors
of their time.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:47.899
Chris Columbus, director of the first two
"Potter" movies, tells audiences during the

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:48.899
reunion:

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:52.040
"I don't think any of the kids had the capability
of understanding the gravity of who they were

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.399
dealing with at the time.

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:55.420
The British royalty of the acting world."

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.860
Among those giant names, one person got a
ton of shoutouts — Coltrane, who shared

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:03.719
a ton of scenes with Radcliffe, Watson, and
Grint in particular.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:04.719
Watson recalled.

00:01:04.719 --> 00:01:09.259
"The adult actors came in and were, like,
the mischief, in a funny way."

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:11.799
Speaking specifically about Coltrane, Grint
said:

00:01:11.799 --> 00:01:18.310
"He was such a kid, like, so immature and
like, just so much fun."

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:22.679
Radcliffe, accompanied by a video of Coltrane
doing a super-silly voice, said:

00:01:22.679 --> 00:01:26.409
"He loved making us laugh, and he was incredibly
good at it."

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:30.509
After that, the reunion brought Watson and
Coltrane together, who shared a hug and snapped

00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:33.369
a photo before reminiscing about their time
on set.

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:37.430
As Watson pointed out, the two spent a lot
of time together filming in Hagrid's hut,

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:41.829
and Coltrane even admitted that he probably
saw the trio more than his own children.

00:01:41.829 --> 00:01:46.619
Even after twenty years, the bond between
Coltrane and the trio was as strong as ever,

00:01:46.619 --> 00:01:51.049
and his, as Watson points out, "warmth and
kindness" made all of the difference for the

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:52.049
young actors.

00:01:52.049 --> 00:01:56.509
Daniel Radcliffe felt so comfortable on the
"Harry Potter" sets with Robbie Coltrane initially

00:01:56.509 --> 00:01:58.590
that he decided to prank his co-star.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:02.239
When appearing on "The Rosie O'Donnell Show"
in the early aughts, Coltrane told the talk

00:02:02.239 --> 00:02:06.299
show host about how Radcliffe got a hold of
his phone and made some adjustments, so he

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:08.020
had no idea how to work it.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.200
A very young Radcliffe was there as the story
was told and couldn't help but chuckle.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.200
Coltrane remembered:

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.500
"This one here turned the language on my cellular
phone into Turkish."

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.950
He then laughed that it would've been easy
to switch it back to English, but you must

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.360
know Turkish to do that.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.470
According to Hollywood.com, Radcliffe felt
terrible about the prank afterward and wrote

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.670
Coltrane a note to apologize.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.720
These types of interviews and the HBO Max
"Harry Potter" reunion special prove just

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.590
how special the late Coltrane was to the rest
of the cast and the fans of the franchise.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.590
Coltrane said:

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.030
"The legacy of the movies is that my children's
generation will show them to their children,

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.850
so you could be watching it in 50 years' time
— easy."

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:51.310
And then, just to make sure no one is exempt
from shedding at least one tear, he poignantly

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:52.310
concluded:

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.810
"I'll not be here, sadly…"

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.470
"...but Hagrid will.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.410
Yes."

